{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-quasi-compact}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e8a0b4030d6c8b487fc499a9a9f2641732d033cb5b4722aa14286413d05ffd25", "source_text": "Quasi-compact objects and colimits", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f3c546a0a6768a7a2254215eadd9bc37801efc2e788b7d8cef76b44abfa55d96", "unit_id": "tag:090G:title"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b500ed95582d15ef2268270a56de9cb4cb4e91f961500f4b9c398e3755a3862", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nTo be able to use the same language as in the case of topological spaces\nwe introduce the following terminology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:51da325a5c4a255d3c71b47327852ea77c18f7f87d28598802bf60ed32464249", "unit_id": "tag:090G:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V_j \\to U\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{V} \\to \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\text{id} : U \\to U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\alpha : J \\to I$", "MATH_0010": "$V_j \\to U_{\\alpha(j)}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0012": "$I$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-morphism-coverings}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:734db2990c86f9083126e04fb85efefc5d292bd72f38b12ad1ef230b9b5f4167", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c7a1f6155a3a7162d9d80b6161804905bd349a1b263010b87a4dd5f4ca10154e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. An object <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-compact<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if given a covering <MATH_0004>\nin <MATH_0005> there exists another covering\n<MATH_0006> and a morphism\n<MATH_0007> of families of maps with fixed target\ngiven by <MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009>, and <MATH_0010>\n(see Definition <REF_0001>)\nsuch that the image of <MATH_0011> is a finite subset of <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe4850da74909a8c88187502830126ab03c575e35887755c83770f394ef197f0", "unit_id": "tag:090H:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9b1a579be81e701f3b3444f9ae9797bfce61c189521134968f0f6e84819a9ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49d7fc3aefde00d6d587d1ef588ad5280f2d8339de36cc77af15670513fe4747", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOf course the usual notion is sufficient to conclude that\n<MATH_0001> is quasi-compact.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e364867c406819e03ff67323923e243721b9ea17af74f7b49c5feefb5310a7b1", "unit_id": "tag:090G:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{V_j \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$I' \\subset I$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I'}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0016": "$\\Rightarrow$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-conclude-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1295d71042f3bd0714e2761afa1b3993fca54d294d0fe4c071f76d1bcf8df1e2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:246465e28b6f5eefe021b4cd425695bf2397edc7ed214c2fdf44194e2c726922", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nConsider the following conditions\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact,\n<STRUCT_0003> for every covering <MATH_0005> in <MATH_0006>\nthere exists a finite covering <MATH_0007>\nof <MATH_0008> refining <MATH_0009>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for every covering <MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011>\nthere exists a finite subset <MATH_0012> such that\n<MATH_0013> is a covering in <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen we always have (3) <MATH_0015> (2) <MATH_0016> (1)\nbut the reverse implications do not hold in general.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c21b4cbf6341cd97000332cbf2fc24be467bc378e1790508412c7eb3250aa66", "unit_id": "tag:0D05:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = [0, 1] \\subset \\mathbf{R}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\epsilon$", "MATH_0003": "$\\delta$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{U \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$X = U = [0, 1]$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-site-topological}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-site}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ef63cfd9af2eb7391f071ebd2a65ddaee5b0ed0e9184d66f702536211bf83b4c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:43e9dced46c0bc3858f3ebb50a573fef74ceace1ac05e36ea1513f49a930b075", "source_text": "The implications are immediate from the definitions.\nLet <MATH_0001>\nas a topological space (with the usual <MATH_0002>-<MATH_0003> topology).\nLet <MATH_0004> be the category of open subspaces of <MATH_0005> with\ninclusions as morphisms and usual open coverings (compare with\nExample <REF_0001>). However, then we change the notion\nof covering in <MATH_0006> to exclude all finite coverings, except\nfor the coverings of the form <MATH_0007>. It is easy to see that this\nwill be a site as in Definition <REF_0002>.\nIn this site the object <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact in the sense of\nDefinition <REF_0003> but <MATH_0009> does not satisfy (2).\nWe leave it to the reader to make an example where (2) holds but not (3).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:de97db06f2952a90b497b314ad90a76eb70dfef3db46ab778ca97e00c38f5daf", "unit_id": "tag:0D05:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b500ed95582d15ef2268270a56de9cb4cb4e91f961500f4b9c398e3755a3862", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the topos theoretic meaning of a quasi-compact object.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:420af1313b54ce91e876774c8698ed5fe9602395587da3e1c7624b79e07c26a5", "unit_id": "tag:090G:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\coprod_{i \\in I} \\mathcal{F}_i \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0006": "$J \\subset I$", "MATH_0007": "$\\coprod_{i \\in J} \\mathcal{F}_i \\to h_U^\\#$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:08c1d5545fa9771d99a75c4d11a496bba87f0638207f2853e56878afc9165581", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8397303798a67dd50676f1e1e7f050d6b66d997de3733ffd0cc869faaa722a3b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every surjection of sheaves\n<MATH_0005>\nthere is a finite subset <MATH_0006> such that\n<MATH_0007> is surjective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:29b56f3f3dccb1ab5a448afaab05bca7478b29fa9dc6ce6ce015a2fa0eca7a7b", "unit_id": "tag:0D06:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\coprod_{i \\in I} \\mathcal{F}_i \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{id}_U$", "MATH_0003": "$h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U_a \\to U\\}_{a \\in A}$", "MATH_0006": "$a \\in A$", "MATH_0007": "$s_a$", "MATH_0008": "$\\coprod_{i \\in I} \\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0009": "$U_a$", "MATH_0010": "$\\text{id}_U$", "MATH_0011": "$a$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{U_{ab} \\to U_a\\}_{b \\in B_a}$", "MATH_0013": "$b \\in B_a$", "MATH_0014": "$\\iota(b) \\in I$", "MATH_0015": "$s_{b}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\iota(b)}$", "MATH_0017": "$U_{ab}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\text{id}_U|_{U_{ab}}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\{U_a \\to U\\}_{a \\in A}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\{U_{ab} \\to U\\}_{a \\in A, b \\in B_a}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\iota : A \\to I$", "MATH_0022": "$a \\in A$", "MATH_0023": "$s_a$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\iota(a)}$", "MATH_0025": "$U_a$", "MATH_0026": "$\\text{id}_U$", "MATH_0027": "$U$", "MATH_0028": "$\\{V_c \\to U\\}_{c \\in C}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\alpha : C \\to A$", "MATH_0030": "$V_c \\to U_{\\alpha(c)}$", "MATH_0031": "$U$", "MATH_0032": "$J = \\Im(\\iota \\circ \\alpha) \\subset I$", "MATH_0033": "$\\coprod_{c \\in C} h_{V_c}^\\# \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0034": "$\\coprod_{i \\in J} \\mathcal{F}_i \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0035": "$h_{V_c}^\\# \\to h_{U_{\\alpha(c)}}\n\\xrightarrow{s_{\\alpha(c)}} \\mathcal{F}_{\\iota(\\alpha(c))} \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0036": "$h_{V_c}^\\# \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0037": "$V_c \\to U$", "MATH_0038": "$s_{\\alpha(c)}$", "MATH_0039": "$\\text{id}_U|_{U_{\\alpha(c)}}$", "MATH_0040": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0041": "$\\coprod_{i \\in I} h_{U_i}^\\# \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0042": "$J \\subset I$", "MATH_0043": "$\\coprod_{j \\in J} h_{U_j}^\\# \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0044": "$\\{V_c \\to U\\}_{c \\in C}$", "MATH_0045": "$U$", "MATH_0046": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0047": "$\\iota : C \\to J$", "MATH_0048": "$\\text{id}_U$", "MATH_0049": "$s_c$", "MATH_0050": "$h_{U_{\\iota(c)}}^\\#$", "MATH_0051": "$V_c$", "MATH_0052": "$s_c \\in h_{U_{\\iota(c)}}(V_c)$", "MATH_0053": "$\\text{id}_U$", "MATH_0054": "$s_c : V_c \\to U_{\\iota(c)}$", "MATH_0055": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-colimit-sheaves}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-covering-surjective-after-sheafification}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-covering-surjective-after-sheafification}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff02616998b707abd2c840a61f11d91ea050a62e141554d78c431d735b04aa9d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b58f36840f06cdf13f9a65ba231f04010369d9461b8ed52b591989d62624071c", "source_text": "Assume (1) and let <MATH_0001>\nbe a surjection. Then <MATH_0002> is a section of\n<MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004>. Hence there exists a covering\n<MATH_0005> and for each <MATH_0006>\na section <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008>\nover <MATH_0009> mapping to <MATH_0010>. By the construction of coproducts as\nsheafification of coproducts of presheaves\n(Lemma <REF_0001>), for each <MATH_0011>\nthere exists a covering <MATH_0012> and\nfor all <MATH_0013> an <MATH_0014> and a section\n<MATH_0015> of <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017>\nmapping to <MATH_0018>. Thus after replacing\nthe covering <MATH_0019> by\n<MATH_0020>\nwe may assume we have a map <MATH_0021>\nand for each <MATH_0022> a section <MATH_0023> of <MATH_0024>\nover <MATH_0025> mapping to <MATH_0026>.\nSince <MATH_0027> is quasi-compact, there is a covering\n<MATH_0028>, a map <MATH_0029>\nwith finite image, and <MATH_0030> over <MATH_0031>.\nThen we see that <MATH_0032> works\nbecause <MATH_0033> is surjective\n(Lemma <REF_0002>)\nand factors through <MATH_0034>.\n(Here we use that the composition\n<MATH_0035>\nis the map <MATH_0036> coming from the morphism\n<MATH_0037> because <MATH_0038> maps to <MATH_0039>.)\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume (2). Let <MATH_0040> be a covering.\nBy Lemma <REF_0003>\nwe see that <MATH_0041> is surjective.\nThus we find a finite subset <MATH_0042> such that\n<MATH_0043> is surjective.\nThen arguing as above we find a covering\n<MATH_0044> of <MATH_0045> in <MATH_0046>\nand a map <MATH_0047>\nsuch that <MATH_0048> lifts to a section\nof <MATH_0049> of <MATH_0050> over <MATH_0051>.\nRefining the covering even further we may assume\n<MATH_0052> mapping to <MATH_0053>.\nThen <MATH_0054> is a morphism over <MATH_0055>\nand we conclude.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:697a6e662ce7655e2e4ca4558a1ca2b079d626b2f91bb99b02a31fae1cae6431", "unit_id": "tag:0D06:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b500ed95582d15ef2268270a56de9cb4cb4e91f961500f4b9c398e3755a3862", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe lemma above motivates the following definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c100d517d9ed5ad334a842d1827f4d8ee57a71e5618f0ba1373afb59cdeabdf7", "unit_id": "tag:090G:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "090G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\coprod_{i \\in I} \\mathcal{F}_i \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$J \\subset I$", "MATH_0006": "$\\coprod_{i \\in J} \\mathcal{F}_i \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "$*$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-quasi-compact-topos}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ffcea799d411a9a110dd245d872df95dfcbf7d61a933c64a638c40161fe10e08", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:274094a2564161619e03e49cde2a7df103469187450a3750dfe2a84224b68a03", "source_text": "An object <MATH_0001> of a topos <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-compact<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif for any surjective map <MATH_0003>\nof <MATH_0004> there exists a finite subset <MATH_0005> such\nthat <MATH_0006> is surjective.\nA topos <MATH_0007> is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0002>quasi-compact<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif its final object <MATH_0008> is a quasi-compact object.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:59ca768f5ddf9187f87f7a5305a07c6657b7e5d4102c795daa4f4b8b6ac5c1a3", "unit_id": "tag:0D07:statement"}
